IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `ea1-part4a-rest-hours`

-- Tests for ea1-part4a-rest-hours.l4 (ss 35 to 41A).  Every expected value is written from
-- the text of the section (inputs/EmA1968.txt) before the function was run.
-- Calendar facts used: 1 February 2026 is a Sunday; so 4 February is a Wednesday, 7 February a Saturday.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 35 Application of this Part to certain workmen and other employees`
-- A monthly pay record: 3000 for the work, 500 overtime, 400 bonus, 100 commission, 50 productivity incentive, 70 travelling allowance, 30 food allowance, 20 housing allowance, 200 other allowances.
-- Salary (s 2(1)) is 3000 + 500 + 400 + 100 + 50 + 30 + 20 + 200 = 4300 (the travelling allowance is out of salary).
-- Taking off overtime, bonus, productivity incentive and the allowances (500 + 400 + 50 + 30 + 20 + 200 = 1200) leaves 3100.
`a monthly pay record` MEANS `Pay for a period` WITH `the amounts are for` IS `Pay is fixed for each month`, `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS 3000, `overtime payments` IS 500, `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS 400, `commissions` IS 100, `productivity incentive payments` IS 50, `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS 0, `travelling allowances` IS 70, `food allowances` IS 30, `housing allowances` IS 20, `allowances of any other kind` IS 200, `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS 0, `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS 0, `value of a travelling concession` IS 0, `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS 0, `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS 0, `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS 0
`a daily pay record` MEANS `Pay for a period` WITH `the amounts are for` IS `Pay is fixed for each day`, `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS 100, `overtime payments` IS 0, `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS 0, `commissions` IS 0, `productivity incentive payments` IS 0, `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS 0, `travelling allowances` IS 0, `food allowances` IS 0, `housing allowances` IS 0, `allowances of any other kind` IS 0, `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS 0, `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS 0, `value of a travelling concession` IS 0, `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS 0, `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS 0, `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS 0
#ASSERT `s 35 the monthly salary measured against the ceiling` `a monthly pay record` EQUALS JUST 3100
#ASSERT `s 35 the monthly salary measured against the ceiling` `a daily pay record` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a): arguments are: a workman, the salary measured, the Minister's substitute for $4,500.
#ASSERT `s 35(a) the workman is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(a)` TRUE (JUST 4500) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(a) the workman is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(a)` TRUE (JUST 4501) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(a) the workman is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(a)` FALSE (JUST 3000) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(a) the workman is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(a)` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(a) the workman is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(a)` TRUE (JUST 4800) (JUST 5000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(a) the workman is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(a)` TRUE (JUST 3100) (JUST 3000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): arguments are: a workman, managerial or executive, the salary measured, the Minister's substitute for $2,600.
#ASSERT `s 35(b) the employee is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(b)` FALSE FALSE (JUST 2600) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35(b) the employee is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(b)` FALSE FALSE (JUST 2601) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(b) the employee is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(b)` TRUE FALSE (JUST 2000) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(b) the employee is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(b)` FALSE TRUE (JUST 2000) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35(b) the employee is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(b)` FALSE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35(b) the employee is one to whom Part 4 applies by virtue of section 35(b)` FALSE FALSE (JUST 2700) (JUST 3000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- both together
#ASSERT `s 35 Part 4 applies to the employee` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35 Part 4 applies to the employee` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35 Part 4 applies to the employee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 35 Part 4 applies to the employee` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 35 Part 4 applies to the employee` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 35 Part 4 applies to the employee` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 36 Rest day`
-- (1): arguments are: allowed a rest day of one whole day without pay in the week, it was a Sunday or another day the employer determined.
#ASSERT `s 36(1) the employer has allowed the employee the rest day in the week` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1) the employer has allowed the employee the rest day in the week` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 36(1) the employer has allowed the employee the rest day in the week` FALSE TRUE)
-- (2): shift work and a continuous period of 30 hours.
#ASSERT `s 36(2) the employer may substitute the continuous period as a rest day` TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36(2) the employer may substitute the continuous period as a rest day` TRUE 36 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36(2) the employer may substitute the continuous period as a rest day` TRUE 29 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 36(2) the employer may substitute the continuous period as a rest day` FALSE 30 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): shift work, begins on a Sunday, the hour (0 to 24) at which it begins: before 6 p.m. is before 18.
#ASSERT `s 36(3) the rest day is deemed to have been granted within the week` TRUE TRUE 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36(3) the rest day is deemed to have been granted within the week` TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 36(3): a period commencing at 6 p.m. is not "before 6 p.m. on a Sunday"; one that does not begin on a Sunday, or an employee not on shift work, leaves the "Where" unmet: no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 36(3) the rest day is deemed to have been granted within the week` TRUE TRUE 18 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 36(3) the rest day is deemed to have been granted within the week` TRUE FALSE 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 36(3) the rest day is deemed to have been granted within the week` FALSE TRUE 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): the rest day is determined by the employer; the roster must be prepared before the month starts (1 March 2026).
#ASSERT `s 36(4) the roster was prepared before the commencement of the month` TRUE (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36(4) the roster was prepared before the commencement of the month` TRUE (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 36(4) the roster was prepared before the commencement of the month` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 36(4) the roster was prepared before the commencement of the month` FALSE (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty, with 10 days to the first of the month: the roster on day 9 is in time, on day 10 is not (read both traces).
#TRACE `s 36(4) the employer's duty to prepare the roster` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 36(4) the employer` DOES `s 36(4) prepare a roster informing the employee of the days appointed to be the employee's rest days in the month` AT 9
#TRACE `s 36(4) the employer's duty to prepare the roster` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 36(4) the employer` DOES `s 36(4) prepare a roster informing the employee of the days appointed to be the employee's rest days in the month` AT 10

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 37 Work on rest day`
-- (1): arguments are: engaged in continuous shift work, the case is one in section 38(2) or 40(2A).
#ASSERT `s 37(1) the employee may be compelled to work on a rest day` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37(1) the employee may be compelled to work on a rest day` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37(1) the employee may be compelled to work on a rest day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 37(1A) the Commissioner has power to decide whether the employee is so engaged` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 37(1A) "In the event of any dispute": no dispute, no power ("in the event of" read as "where": fork F-EVENT).
#ASSERT `s 37(1A) the Commissioner has power to decide whether the employee is so engaged` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3A)(a): normal hours; 8 if nothing is agreed.
#ASSERT `s 37(3A)(a) the normal hours of work per day` NOTHING 8 EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `s 37(3A)(a) the normal hours of work per day` (JUST 7) 8 EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `s 37(3A)(a) the normal hours of work per day` (JUST 9) 8 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(3A)(a) the normal hours of work per day` (JUST 9) 9 EQUALS JUST 9
#ASSERT `s 37(3A)(b) the employee's hourly basic rate of pay` (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `s 37(3A)(b) the employee's hourly basic rate of pay` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): own request.  Normal hours 8; a day's basic rate 100; an hour's basic rate 20.
-- arguments are: hours worked, normal hours, the day rate, the hourly rate, a written order under 41A(2).
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 3 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 4 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 5 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 8 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
-- 9 hours: one day (100) and 1.5 x 20 for the one hour over (30).
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 9 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 130
-- 9.5 hours: "each hour or part thereof": 2 hours over, 2 x 30.
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 9.5 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 160
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 3 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 3 8 NOTHING (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 9 8 (JUST 100) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(2) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employee's own request` 9 8 NOTHING (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the employer's request.
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 3 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 5 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 8 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 9 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 230
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 9.5 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS JUST 260
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 3 8 (JUST 100) (JUST 20) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 3 8 NOTHING (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 5 8 NOTHING (JUST 20) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(3) the least sum payable for the rest day worked at the employer's request` 9 8 (JUST 100) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4)
#ASSERT `s 37(4) subsection (3) applies to the employee` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 37(4) subsection (3) applies to the employee` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(4) the employer must give the employee a day or part of a day off in substitution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 37(4) the employer must give the employee a day or part of a day off in substitution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 37(4) the employer must give the employee a day or part of a day off in substitution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 38 Hours of work`
-- (1) the limit of hours in a day: arguments are: (d) fewer than 8 hours on some days by agreement, (e) not more than 5 days a week by agreement, subsection (9) takes the employee out, a 41A(1) order.
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one day` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 9
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one day` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 9
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one day` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one day` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the limit in a week: arguments are: (f) every alternate week less than 44 by agreement, subsection (9), a 41A(1) order.
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one week` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 44
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one week` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 48
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one week` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(1) the limit of hours in one week` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a), (c): consecutive hours without leisure: 6, or 8 for continuous work with at least 45 minutes for a meal.
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(a) the limit of consecutive hours without a period of leisure` TRUE 45 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(a) the limit of consecutive hours without a period of leisure` TRUE 44 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(a) the limit of consecutive hours without a period of leisure` FALSE 60 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(a) the employee may be required to work the consecutive hours` 6 6 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(a) the employee may be required to work the consecutive hours` 7 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 38(1) proviso (c): work carried on continuously with the meal opportunity "may be required to work for 8 consecutive hours": inside the grant.
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(a) the employee may be required to work the consecutive hours` 8 8 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(a) the employee may be required to work the consecutive hours` 9 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): the day and the week against the limits.
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the day` 8 (JUST 8) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the day` 9 (JUST 8) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 38(1) provisos (d), (e): "the limit of 8 hours in one day may be exceeded", up to 9 hours: inside the grant.
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the day` 9 (JUST 9) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the day` 10 (JUST 9) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the day` 10 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the week` 44 (JUST 44) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the week` 45 (JUST 44) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 38(1) proviso (f): "the limit of 44 hours in one week may be exceeded in the other week", up to 48 hours: inside the grant.
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the week` 48 (JUST 48) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the week` 49 (JUST 48) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(b) the employee may be required to work the hours in the week` 49 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (f): 88 hours in any continuous period of 2 weeks.
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(f) the limit of hours in any continuous period of 2 weeks` TRUE EQUALS JUST 88
#ASSERT `s 38(1)(f) the limit of hours in any continuous period of 2 weeks` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the six cases.
#ASSERT `s 38(2) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` `s 38(2)(a) accident, actual or threatened` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(2) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` `s 38(2)(b) work, the performance of which is essential to the life of the community` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(2) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` `s 38(2)(c) work essential for defence or security` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(2) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` `s 38(2)(d) urgent work to be done to machinery or plant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(2) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` `s 38(2)(e) an interruption of work which it was impossible to foresee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(2) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` `s 38(2)(f) work to be performed by employees in any industrial undertaking essential to the economy of Singapore or any of the essential services as defined under Part 3 of the Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 38(2) the employer may require the employee to exceed the limit of hours in subsection (1) and to work on a rest day` `s 38(2) some other case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(3) the Commissioner has power to decide whether the employer is justified` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 38(3) "In the event of any dispute": no dispute, no power (fork F-EVENT).
#ASSERT `s 38(3) the Commissioner has power to decide whether the employer is justified` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): 3 hours of overtime at an hourly basic rate of 20: 1.5 x 20 x 3 = 90; 2.5 hours: 75.
-- arguments are: the hours of overtime, the hourly rate, at the employer's request, a written order under 41A(2).
#ASSERT `s 38(4) the least payment for the extra work` (JUST 3) (JUST 20) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 90
#ASSERT `s 38(4) the least payment for the extra work` (JUST 2.5) (JUST 20) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 75
#ASSERT `s 38(4) the least payment for the extra work` (JUST 3) (JUST 20) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(4) the least payment for the extra work` (JUST 3) (JUST 20) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(4) the least payment for the extra work` NOTHING (JUST 20) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(4) the least payment for the extra work` (JUST 3) NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): 72 hours a month.
#ASSERT `s 38(5) the employee may be permitted to work the overtime in the month` 72 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(5) the employee may be permitted to work the overtime in the month` 73 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6)
#ASSERT `s 38(6) the hourly basic rate of pay for calculating the payment due for overtime` (JUST 18) EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `s 38(6) the hourly basic rate of pay for calculating the payment due for overtime` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8): 12 hours in a day, except in the cases of (2)(a) to (e).
#ASSERT `s 38(8) the employee may work the hours in the day` 13 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(8) the employee may work the hours in the day` 13 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 38(8) the employee may work the hours in the day` 12 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9)
#ASSERT `s 38(9) section 38 applies to the employee` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 38(9) section 38 applies to the employee` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

